  "summary": "The study compares four free-standing Ti3C2Tx films: untreated Ti3C2Tx and Mn-, Ni-, or Co-acetate-treated Ti3C2Tx\u2212M films. Acetate treatment is reported to intercalate metal ions, enlarge the interlayer spacing, and create porous MXene nanosheets. Ti3C2Tx\u2212Ni gives the highest explicitly printed CV capacitance, 369 F g\u22121 at 2 mV s\u22121, whereas Ti3C2Tx\u2212Mn is the headline rate/cycling performer, beginning at 358 F g\u22121 at 10 A g\u22121 and retaining 248 F g\u22121 after 100 000 cycles at 100 A g\u22121. The Mn material was also used in a symmetric PVA\u2212H2SO4 solid-state device, but this is not counted separately because it uses the same electrode material. SSA, porosity percentage, and most non-Mn thickness/loading values are not printed in the supplied text."
}